INT. DEFUNCT BUS DEPOT - NIGHT

Cracked tile. Bench seating, rusted. A flickering departure board with no destinations.

Six masked figures enter through a loading door. They fan out. MATEUS SOTO (40s, the crew lead) raises a fist. Behind him, DESIREE "DEZI" MOULTRIE (30s) hauls a duffel; her brother JULIEN MOULTRIE (20s) props open the door; HUGO BRANDTNER (50s) unrolls a map on a bench; AGNES LOVELACE (60s) lifts a crowbar; and the kid, PADDY GLASS (19), keeps lookout, twitching.

MATEUS
(to the group)
Eyes up. Nobody moves until I say.

DEZI
(to Julien)
Stop jiggling the door.

JULIEN
Sorry.

HUGO
(to himself)
East wall. East wall.

AGNES
Where's the vault?

MATEUS
Under the baggage claim.

PADDY
There's no baggage claim.

MATEUS
Under where it used to be.

Agnes sets the crowbar against a locker, strides to the broken department board, and swings. The glass shatters; behind it, a steel panel. She grins.

AGNES
Found it.

Hugo scribbles on the map. Julien lets the door swing shut and hurries over. Dezi opens the duffel, pulls out a drill and a coil of cable. Paddy glances at the street, then back, then at the street again.

PADDY
Headlights.

MATEUS
Everybody down!

They drop behind benches, lockers, pillars. A pair of headlights sweeps the windows and slides past. Nobody breathes. The engine fades.

PADDY
False alarm.

DEZI
(muttering)
Kid's going to give me a heart attack.

MATEUS
(to the group)
Back to work. Fifteen minutes.
